From 72bf66f9bff21656f3bb7a7cac0ff9c2a34c073d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:56:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(project): a loaded stock keeps its geometry revision

set_facets bumps an entity's geometry revision on every landing. The
project loader pinned it back to the file's value for models but not for
stocks, so a stock set twice saved "rev": 2, loaded as rev 1, and the
re-save differed from the file it was opened from. The Stock arm now pins
rev after set_facets, unconditionally like the Model arm (an absent key
pins 0, matching older files). Staleness never reads rev; this removes
file-byte churn on open-and-save.

Pinned by project_roundtrip::stock_set_twice_keeps_its_rev_across_save_load_save.

Fixes #340

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
